{"explanation":"Strengthen the existing unchanged-MasterKey-entry-point regression test so an incorrect password must produce the established concrete AES/GCM authentication failure rather than allowing a successful decrypt to pass silently. The existing round-trip encoding and AES-algorithm assertions remain unchanged.","review_assumptions":["The supported Android crypto provider continues to report an incorrect AES/GCM password-derived wrapping key as AEADBadTagException, as the existing test already expects.","The coordinated MasterKey implementation preserves its generate(String) and decrypt(String) entry points and continues to expose AES key material after successful decryption."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"high","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/MasterKeyTest.java","original_code":"    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String pwd = "MyM4sterPassw0rd";
        String wrongpwd = "Incorrectpwd";

        MasterKey orig = MasterKey.generate(pwd);
        MasterKey read = new Gson().fromJson(new Gson().toJson(orig), MasterKey.class);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded(), read.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded());
        assertEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");
        assertEquals(read.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");

        try {
            orig.decrypt(wrongpwd);
        } catch (AEADBadTagException e) {
            // Expected
            // javax.crypto.AEADBadTagException:
            // error:1e000065:Cipher functions:OPENSSL_internal:BAD_DECRYPT
        }
    }","edit_kind":"test","corrected_code":"    @Test
    public void test() throws GeneralSecurityException, IOException {
        String pwd = "MyM4sterPassw0rd";
        String wrongpwd = "Incorrectpwd";

        MasterKey orig = MasterKey.generate(pwd);
        MasterKey read = new Gson().fromJson(new Gson().toJson(orig), MasterKey.class);

        Assert.assertArrayEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded(), read.decrypt(pwd).getEncoded());
        assertEquals(orig.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");
        assertEquals(read.decrypt(pwd).getAlgorithm(), "AES");

        try {
            orig.decrypt(wrongpwd);
            Assert.fail("Decrypting with an incorrect password must fail authentication");
        } catch (AEADBadTagException e) {
            // Expected
            // javax.crypto.AEADBadTagException:
            // error:1e000065:Cipher functions:OPENSSL_internal:BAD_DECRYPT
        }
    }","reason":"Retains the existing successful MasterKey serialization, decryption, key-encoding, and AES-algorithm assertions while making the existing wrong-password AES/GCM authentication expectation enforceable." ,"symbol":"MasterKeyTest existing MasterKey construction/use cases"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["MasterKeyTest retains the existing public test() signature and exercises the unchanged MasterKey.generate(String) and decrypt(String) entry points.","MasterKeyTest preserves the existing decrypted-key encoding and AES-algorithm assertions across JSON serialization.","MasterKeyTest now requires an incorrect password to fail with AEADBadTagException."],"required_contracts":["MasterKey retains its existing generate(String) and decrypt(String) public entry points, checked-exception behavior, PBKDF2 metadata, and persisted encrypted-key representation.","MasterKey supplies an AES KeyGenerator-origin key to EncryptedKey.encrypt while retaining the existing caller-facing EncryptedKey.encrypt signature.","EncryptedKey continues to retain AES/GCM parameters and authenticate the protected-key algorithm as AAD for compatible decryption."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/MasterKeyTest.java","required_tests":["Run MasterKeyTest on supported Android providers and verify successful MasterKey JSON round-trip decryption preserves key bytes and the AES algorithm.","Verify decrypting the generated MasterKey with an incorrect password raises AEADBadTagException.","Run the coordinated EncryptedKeyTest and KeyStoreAccessTest instrumentation coverage after applying the related AES/GCM lifecycle edits."]}
